  "scope": {
    "platform": "Darwin arm64",
    "profile": "Local signed native QUIC plus public HTTP administration and the public Rust SDK. Real synthetic PCMU/PCMA media flows on actual managed Connections. EdDSA and ES256 default lifecycle/quality and endpoint revocation; EdDSA codec replacement and owned selection replay. Provider backpressure uses the existing designated loopback fixture; no real account or remote media is contacted."
  },
  "schema_version": 81,
  "pinned_patches": 131,
  "upstream_edits": false,
  "store_schema_edits": false,
  "implementation": [
    "Runtime Physical owns its independent NativeLifecycleMux, and CanonicalHandler fairly multiplexes its lifecycle delivery with Conversation subscriptions. After exact signed negotiation and durable original resource capture, the host registers current-source metadata rather than retaining the offer invocation or idle authority readers.",
    "Each event tries fresh original-source NativeMediaRead under Store fences and validates exact Core/wire Conversation, Session and Connection, original Identity, participant epoch, Device, Endpoint, ownership key, credential and generation. It checks the current media owner and original activation. Contention waits without a reader; actual engine admission/write retains the guard within the existing one-second IO bound and original source/physical/runtime lifetime.",
    "The pinned engine separately fences actual flow, controller revision and exact bindings through reliable IO. connection.ready and stream.opened follow observed negotiated-direction flow. Codec replacement closes its old announced binding and only opens the replacement after actual flow. These are scoped hints, not journal facts or operation completion.",
    "Default five-second quality contains actual accepted packet/byte counts and derived bitrate. Unmeasured loss, jitter, RTT and MOS stay absent. A wrong or expired origin cannot borrow another Connection or successor authority.",
    "PublicNativeAudio selector control reads the wire and preserves unrelated frames in the bounded SDK inbox, rather than consuming queued events recursively or treating another scope as its parameter request or result. Exact original operation replay and revision remain unchanged. Low-level receive remains an event API; control-only test fixtures explicitly consume lifecycle hints and dedicated lifecycle cases inspect raw verified frames."
  ],
  "actual_cases": [
    {
      "name": "canonical_native_connections::lifecycle::production_native_lifecycle_quality_reports_actual_flow_through_signed_sdk",
      "behavior": "Both EdDSA and ES256: a reliable heartbeat after offer/admission sees no readiness without media. Actual duplex audio precedes exact ready/opened handles and measured sent/received counts. A correlated SDK operation request preserves unsolicited events in its inbox. Public administrator SDK revokes the actual target Connection Endpoint by CAS within three seconds; its credential remains current. Heartbeat barriers through another complete quality cadence observe no freshly created event after revocation, while the independent peer receives a new current quality interval."
    },
    {
      "name": "canonical_native_connections::lifecycle::production_native_lifecycle_closes_original_codec_binding_and_opens_only_observed_replacement",
      "behavior": "An actual target PCMU stream is first opened after duplex flow. Public signed codec control negotiates a different PCMA handle and durable result. Real FFmpeg decoding proves media in both directions. Raw verified lifecycle facts close the original logical binding with codec-renegotiated before opening the exact replacement handle/codec; every event retains the original own wire scope without an operation ID or reply correlation."
    },
    {
      "name": "canonical_native_connections::lifecycle::production_owned_native_audio_selection_replay_preserves_pending_lifecycle_events",
      "behavior": "Public prepare_public_native_audio and subscribe_audio negotiate an owned peer against an actual raw signed source. Continuous20ms producers and cancellation-safe atomic datagram probes observe marked audio both ways. Signaling stays unread through a full quality cadence; repeating the exact original selection operation/revision succeeds, preserves revision2 and leaves owned sending usable."
    }
  ],
